# shir_nodes/cut_at.node — expression-level semantic IR node.
# CutAt: cut `text` at ONE occurrence of `delim` — the four single-star
# glob-strip identities that are pure find()/rfind() work:
#
#   ${v%%lit*}   keep the head BEFORE the first  occurrence  (head,  first)
#   ${v%lit*}    keep the head BEFORE the last   occurrence  (head,  !first)
#   ${v#*lit}    keep the tail AFTER  the first  occurrence  (!head, first)
#   ${v##*lit}   keep the tail AFTER  the last   occurrence  (!head, !first)
#
# No match leaves the text unchanged (bash's strip is a no-op when the
# pattern does not match). `delim` is a magic-free literal (the fold
# refuses `*`/`?`/`[`/`\` bodies): `is_magic_free`.
#
# The identities are THEOREMS, not an appeal to glob semantics:
# docs/fm/TextOps/ShIR_TextOps_Cut.thy proves `find_first`/`rfind_last`
# (a returned index is an occurrence, none means no occurrence anywhere,
# leftmost/maximal) and, over arbitrary text and literal, `cut_at_sound`
# (each form is take/drop at its own occurrence, text unchanged on no
# match) and `affix_strip_fold_sound` (the fold's contract: all four star
# shapes at those primitives, plus the plain branch at either end —
# `#lit*` is AffixStrip's strip_prefix, `%*lit` its strip_suffix, the
# latter via `cut_head_last_at_trail`). What is NOT modelled is the glob
# engine itself: "shortest/longest match of `lit*`" is identified with the
# first/last occurrence of the literal, and that identification is
# assumed, not proved (docs/fm/README.md). The AST reading was checked
# against bash before the node was written, but the identities now rest on
# the theory rather than on that check.
#
# Emitted by the `affix-strip-fold` transform (the star-form branch; the
# plain-literal branch keeps using AffixStrip).
#
# Backends: Rust (find/rfind + slicing), C (one strstr find + a vbuf
#   copy — see c_backend's ext_value_c CutAt arm) — target-gated offers;
#   other backends accept by adding a render arm and their target to the
#   gate (the FieldGrab offer pattern).
# Fallback: sh2.cutAt(text, delim, head, first)

node CutAt
tag "CutAt"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field text: expr
field delim: string
field head: bool
field first: bool
spec: TextOps#cut_at_sound
